// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CentralComputerClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P680427436" "The Central Computer"
// DetailString :
"P1687698603" "Doctor Keppel informed you that the network has been disconnected from the console workstations, but if you could access the central computer then you can find the location of Lady Gallant's prison cell."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LadyGallantLocationClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1031948058" "Lady Gallant's Locationl"
// DetailString :
"P3887234929" "According to the central computer, Lady Gallant's prison cell is located in Ward 11."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1252084441" "A Squire's Charge"
// DetailString :
"P3963988896" "Scarlet Squire was unsure of where her mentor, Lady Gallant, was held after they both went through the rift in Galaxy City. She asked you to talk to Doctor Keppel for ideas and the scientist informed you that the master computer beneath the enclosure would hold the answers. You decended back into the bowels of the enclosure and fought through waves of clockwork defenders. Once you found the computer you accessed the prison records and located Lady Gallant's holding cell. Returning to Scarlet Squire you gave her the news and for the first time saw her smile."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LadyGallantCellClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P544453657" "Writing on the Wall"
// DetailString :
"P661885105" "Carved into the steel alloy of the cell wall is a brief message. It reads thusly.<br><br><color lightseagreen>S.S.<br>Escaped. Way past shield.<br>Wait. Come back for you.<br><span align=right>-G</span></color><br><br>You can only assume the initials stand for Scarlet Squire and that G stands for Lady Gallant. As far as you can tell, she escaped and found a way past the Enclosure's shield."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2602093613" "Scarlet Squire was unsure of where her mentor, Lady Gallant, was held after they both went through the rift in Galaxy City. She asked you to talk to Doctor Keppel for ideas and the scientist informed you that the master computer beneath the enclosure would hold the answers. You decended back into the bowels of the enclosure and fought through waves of clockwork defenders. Once you found the computer you accessed the prison records and located Lady Gallant's holding cell. Returning to Scarlet Squire you gave her the news and for the first time saw her smile.<br><br>Scarlet Squire asked you to return to the Praetorian holding cells and rescue her mentor, Lady Gallant. Battling through the clockwork garrison, you made your way to the cell block only to find that Lady Gallant was already gone. In her place you discovered a message carved by sword point into the steel walls and addressed to her squire. You relayed the message to Scarlet, informing her that Lady Gallant had apparently found her own way out, and, furthermore, a way outside of the Rift Enclosure."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LadyGallantFightingClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1586699787" "An Evicerated Devoured"
// DetailString :
"P3744914821" "This devoured was expertly dispatched by a sword. This must be the work of Lady Gallant."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LadyGallantWoundedClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3755592023" "Claws of Crimson"
// DetailString :
"P506913233" "The claws of this slain devoured are still wet with human blood, while a trail of crimson leads deeper into the woods. Lady Gallant appears to have been seriously injured."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LadyGallantCrippledClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3846642161" "Blood Soaked Garments"
// DetailString :
"P165248482" "Blood soaked strips of Lady Gallant's costume lay around the still twitching body of this slain devoured. You are not far behind Lady Gallant now, but you begin to fear that you may be too late."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LadyGallantSwordClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P307174520" "Paramour, the Gallant Blade "
// DetailString :
"P3942001490" "There was nothing you could do to save Lady Gallant from her ignoble fate than release her from the evil that consumed her. You recovered this, her magic sword, intent on delivering it to Scarlet Squire so that Lady Gallant's memory will never die."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL2-9_RE_ASquiresCharge_StoryArc_SouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P436367293" "Whenever you look at this dainty shred of fabric from Lady Gallant's outfit you cannot help but think of it as her favor, but then your thoughts innevitably turn to Praetoria and Lady Gallant's ignoble end which you've come to call <color deepskyblue>A Squire's Charge</color>.<br><br>Scarlet Squire was unsure of where her mentor, Lady Gallant, was held after they both went through the rift in Galaxy City. She asked you to talk to Doctor Keppel for ideas and the scientist informed you that the master computer beneath the enclosure would hold the answers. You decended back into the bowels of the enclosure and fought through waves of clockwork defenders. Once you found the computer you accessed the prison records and located Lady Gallant's holding cell. Returning to Scarlet Squire you gave her the news and for the first time saw her smile.<br><br>Scarlet Squire asked you to return to the Praetorian holding cells and rescue her mentor, Lady Gallant. Battling through the clockwork garrison, you made your way to the cell block only to find that Lady Gallant was already gone. In her place you discovered a message carved by sword point into the steel walls and addressed to her squire. You relayed the message to Scarlet, informing her that Lady Gallant had apparently found her own way out, and, furthermore, a way outside of the Rift Enclosure.<br><br>Distraught, but loyal, Scarlet Squire agreed to her mentor's wishes and stayed put, but she wasn't about to give up looking for her. She begged you to venture beyond the Rift Enclosure's shield and look for Lady Gallant. You left the protection of the shield and entered the Praetorian forest. It was there, in the wilderness, that you discovered the reason for the shield surrounding the Rift Enclosure; the Devouring Earth. The forest seemed to swarm with the creatures, and, after not too long, you came across evidence of another battling their way through them, it was Lady Gallant.<br><br>Hot on her trail of carnage you found mounting evidence that she had been seriously wounded by her foes, and then, you found her. Her wounds proved too grievious and she had succumbed to her enemies. You could barely supress the mounting horror as you realized that Lady Gallant had become one of the Devoured. You had no choice now but to fight for your life and avenge Lady Gallant's memory. In the end, you gave her the peaceful rest she deserved, and solemnly recovered her sword, Paramour, to return to her loyal squire.<br><br>Scarlet Squire was overcome with grief, but, like you, she took a measure of comfort in knowing that Lady Gallant's memory would be remain pure and untarnished. With Paramour in hand, Scarlet Squire looked forward to the path that lay ahead. Her mentor's teachings would not be forgotten, and Paramour would not find rest anytime soon, for there was still good to be done, and Lady Scarlet aimed to do it."

